Edge: BLOCKED may be due to pending required checks (fresh head). Resolving suggestion threads then is still fine (they're approved-with-suggestions machine threads; the merge gate still waits for checks). But is it right to resolve threads while the head might still change? Threads on an approved head — pr_approved is sticky; the verdict record is for the current head. If head moves, pr_approved stays (sticky) and the verdict record lookup for the new head fails → gate closed. In decideActions BLOCKED branch, state.pr.headSha is the current head; resolve uses records for that exact head. Safe.

